              "locked": false,
              "content": {
                "html": "<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">If you or someone you care for has been referred for a nuclear medicine scan or treatment, it's natural to have questions.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">This section has been created to help you understand what nuclear medicine is, what to expect during your appointment and where to find reliable information before and after your visit.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\">Whether you're attending for your first scan, supporting a family member or looking for information about a specific procedure, you'll find a range of trusted resources to help you feel informed and reassured.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"font-size: 20px;\"><strong>Please note:</strong> The British Nuclear Medicine Society cannot provide individual medical advice. If you have questions about your appointment or treatment, please contact your Nuclear Medicine Department, the clinician who referred you or your GP.</span></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p>",
                "colorRole": "default",
